description:
Model a small lending library with classes, records, inheritance and an interface. Dates are `DateOnly` values, always passed in, so the code never reads the clock.

```csharp
public record Book(string Isbn, string Title, string Author);

public abstract class Member(string id, string name)
{
    public string Id { get; }            // as given
    public string Name { get; }
    public decimal FinesOwed { get; }    // can only be changed by the library (internal or protected setter)
    public abstract int MaxLoans { get; }
    public abstract int LoanDays { get; }
    public virtual decimal FinePerDay => 0.25m;
}
public class Adult(string id, string name) : Member    // 5 loans, 21 days
public class Child(string id, string name) : Member    // 3 loans, 14 days, 0.10 per day

public record Loan(Member Member, Book Book, DateOnly Due);

public class Library
{
    public void AddBook(Book book, int copies = 1)
    public void AddMember(Member member)
    public Loan Borrow(string memberId, string isbn, DateOnly today)
    public decimal Return(string memberId, string isbn, DateOnly today)   // the fine for this loan
    public int Available(string isbn)
    public IReadOnlyList<Loan> LoansOf(string memberId)                  // in the order borrowed
    public List<string> Overdue(DateOnly today)
    public void PayFine(string memberId, decimal amount)
}
```

**Rules**
- `AddBook` adds copies (adding the same ISBN again adds to its copies); `copies` must be 1 or more (`ArgumentOutOfRangeException`). `AddMember` throws an `ArgumentException` for an id already in use.
- `Borrow` returns the new loan, due `LoanDays` after `today`. It throws an `InvalidOperationException` with exactly one of these messages, checked in this order:
  `unknown member <id>`, `unknown book <isbn>`, `unpaid fines`, `loan limit reached`, `already borrowed` (the member has this book already), `no copies available`.
- `Return` throws `InvalidOperationException("no such loan")` when that member does not have that book. Otherwise it removes the loan and returns the fine: days after the due date × `FinePerDay`, at most 10.00. The fine is added to the member's `FinesOwed`.
- A member who owes anything cannot borrow until they pay. `PayFine` lowers `FinesOwed` by the amount; it throws an `ArgumentOutOfRangeException` if the amount is 0 or less or more than is owed.
- `Overdue(today)` lists loans with `today` after the due date as `"<name>: <title> (<days> days)"` (`1 day` for one), most days first, then by name and title (ordinal).

